<title>BELGIUM: EU seeks to cut 1997/98 rice storage increments.</title>
<headline>EU seeks to cut 1997/98 rice storage increments.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission on Wednesday proposed that the monthly increase in rice storage payments be cut by 12 percent to 2.0 Ecus a tonne in 1997/98 (September/August).</p>
<p>The intervention price for paddy rice would be cut by five percent to 333.45 Ecus a tonne.</p>
<p>EU Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler was expected to present the proposal, part of the 1997/98 farm price package, to farm ministers on March 17-18 and they were due to take a decision by end-June.</p>
</text>
